WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:13,850
Is the ketogenic diet critical for bladder cancer?

00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:16,850
Typically, no.

00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:19,850
I don't know.

00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:21,850
The person asks this question, I don't know.

00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:27,850
What we tested you on is the cause or the dietary driver of your cancer.

00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:32,850
But certainly, even if you've been following that well and your cancer is growing,

00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:39,850
there's certainly nothing wrong with trying a different diet and going on, you know, ketogenic is,

00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:45,850
I wouldn't say it's necessarily a radical diet, but it's a much more difficult diet to follow.

00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:48,850
But it's certainly nothing wrong with going on.

00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:52,850
Nobody's going to be injured by going on a ketogenic diet.

00:00:52,850 --> 00:01:00,850
The only thing that I would say is if we found that your cancer is driven by proteins,

00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:03,850
typically a ketogenic diet is going to be high in protein.

00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:06,850
So you do our risky, you know, that.

00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:11,850
But again, if your cancer is growing and you want to make some changes,

00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:17,850
cancer can morph and change, and sometimes it's good to try a different diet like that

00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:22,850
and give it a try for a month and see if there's any shrinkage of the cancer,

00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:26,850
because cancer is constantly trying to morph and change its fuel source.

00:01:26,850 --> 00:01:32,850
So I don't think there's anything wrong with trying to ketogenic diet if your cancer is going the wrong way.

